{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>By the blessing of</b> — attached to the word above [i.e., the preceding phrase]. And so it is fitting that they [the righteous] rejoice, for by the blessing of the righteous a city is exalted, meaning they raise up its buildings; or it alludes to its people. And <b>by the mouth of the wicked</b> — who testifies falsely, or the talebearing — is destroyed, [as in] ובעבור פי רשע תהרס קריתם [\"and by the mouth of the wicked their city is destroyed\"]."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is unusually compressed; I read the structure as Ibn Ezra citing the lemma בברכת, then glossing it via three parallel interpretive options. The final phrase appears to be his own Hebrew paraphrase/restatement of the verse's second half."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:10.096212549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}